c Graph H_8 of Theorem 1 in 'The CLIQUES Algorithm Is Not Output-Polynomial' (Sec. 3)
c target n = 200; nearest H_k has n = 2k^2+9k = 200 vertices (k = 8)
c maximal cliques: 1585 (Lemma bound (k+1)(2k(k+3)+1) = 1593 <= n^2 = 40000)
c every run of CLIQUES makes at least 2^(k+1)-1 = 511 recursive calls (one run with min-label tie-breaking and increasing order: 13872)
c vertices: guards g_i = 1..8; core a_i = k+2i-1, b_i = k+2i (9..24); witnesses 25..200, 11 per core vertex in the order a_1, b_1, a_2, ...
p edge 200 4280
